# The windowed app in game (run_app.py; Metal; not part of --menus, which is
# headless): Escape through the intro movies, Single Player, Play Random Map,
# Start Game with legion's parity settings (800x600x32; run_app.py turns on
# custom civilizations, so no "Choose Civilization" comes first), then the
# game with nobody at the controls: 10 seconds still, then Up held for 2 s and
# Down for 2 s with the pointer in the middle of the map (no edge scrolling).
# run_app.py reads the app's own frame stats (the guest's presents a second at
# 800x600) and, from the input probe, how evenly the camera moved from frame
# to frame (tools/input/evenness.py). See ../settings.script for the pointer.
timeout 400000
pointer f32 [0x9197a8]+4 [0x9197a8]+8
hold 250
wait frames 30
key ESCAPE
wait 2500
key ESCAPE
wait 2500
key ESCAPE
wait size 1024 768 within 180000
wait 3000
moveby 1 1
wait 300
click 511 268                 # Single Player
wait change within 15000
wait 1000
click 748 145                 # Play Random Map
wait change within 20000
wait 1500
click 644 730                 # Start Game
wait size 800 600 within 60000
wait 2500
mark
wait change 0.5 within 240000 # the loading screen gives way to the game
wait 5000
move 400 300
wait 10000
log hold Up
key UP down
wait 2000
key UP up
wait 1000
log hold Down
key DOWN down
wait 2000
key DOWN up
wait 1000
dump app-frame-limit
quit
